---
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import Showcase from "../../../components/Showcase.astro";

const html = `<span data-sk-icon="search" data-sk-icon-size="lg"></span>
<span data-sk-icon="settings" data-sk-icon-size="lg"></span>
<span data-sk-icon="warning" data-sk-icon-size="lg"></span>
<span data-sk-icon="check" data-sk-icon-size="lg"></span>
<span data-sk-icon="close" data-sk-icon-size="lg"></span>`;

const react = `import { Icon } from "@skryensya/react/icon";

<Icon name="search" size="lg" />
<Icon name="settings" size="lg" />
<Icon name="warning" size="lg" />
<Icon name="check" size="lg" />
<Icon name="close" size="lg" />;`;

const sizeHtml = `<span data-sk-icon="check" data-sk-icon-size="sm"></span>
<span data-sk-icon="check"></span>
<span data-sk-icon="check" data-sk-icon-size="lg"></span>`;

const sizeReact = `import { Icon } from "@skryensya/react/icon";

<Icon name="check" size="sm" />
<Icon name="check" />
<Icon name="check" size="lg" />;`;

const vanilla = `<!-- Geometry outside the set: you write it. -->
<svg
  class="sk-icon"
  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
  fill="none"
  stroke="currentColor"
  stroke-width="2"
  aria-hidden="true"
  focusable="false"
>
  <path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" />
</svg>`;

const vanillaHydrate = `<!-- You write the name of the role, not the <svg>. -->
<span data-sk-icon="chevron-down"></span>
<span data-sk-icon="close" data-sk-icon-label="Cerrar"></span>`;

const vanillaBind = `import { mountIcons } from "@skryensya/vanilla/icon";
import { lucideIcons } from "@skryensya/icons-lucide";

// replace each [data-sk-icon] with the <svg> of the set. The
// set is explicit.
mountIcons(document, lucideIcons);`;

const reactApi = `import { Icon } from "@skryensya/react/icon";

// no settings: draw with Phosphor, the default set
<Icon name="chevron-down" />
{/* a system role */}
<Icon name="close" label="Cerrar" />
{/* means something alone → role="img" */}
<Icon data={sparkle} />
{/* off the set, the only opt-in */}`;

const provider = `import { IconSetProvider, Icon } from "@skryensya/react/icon";
import { lucideIcons } from "@skryensya/icons-lucide";

// another set? you bind it once, at the root, just like
// you choose a brand
<IconSetProvider set={lucideIcons}>
  <App />
</IconSetProvider>;`;

const sizesCss = `/* another size? the hook is redeclared, like any value
   system arbitrary */
.hero .sk-icon { --sk-icon-size: 2rem; }`;
---

<Base
  title="Icon"
  description="Icon: the sk-icon pattern in React and vanilla — roles of vocabulary, proper geometry, sizes and a11y in the call site."
>
  <h1>Icon</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    How do you put an icon on the screen: <code>&lt;Icon&gt;</code> in React,
    <code>data-sk-icon</code> + <code>mountIcons</code> in vanilla, or the
    <code>&lt;svg class="sk-icon"&gt;</code> a mano. El vocabulario de roles, los sets como marca y por
    qué el CSS no toca fill/stroke están en <a href="/en/icons">Iconography</a>.
  </p>

  <Showcase html={html} react={react} label="Icon" />

  <h2>React</h2>
  <p>
    <code>Icon</code> takes <code>name</code> <strong>or</strong> <code>data</code>, never both.
    <code>name</code> is a portable role that survives a set change; <code>data</code> is
    your geometry, purposefully coupled and visible on the call site.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={reactApi} label="React" note="React renders (decision 14)" />
  <p>
    <code>&lt;Icon name="…"&gt;</code> draws without configuration: Phosphor travels with
    <code>@skryensya/react</code>. For another set, you install it and wrap the app once.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={provider} label="change the default set" note="Lucide/Material child opt-in" />

  <h2>Vanilla: hydrate by name, or write the markup</h2>
  <p>
    <code>mountIcons(root, set)</code> replaces a placeholder with the <strong>name</strong> of the role
    by the same <code>&lt;svg class="sk-icon"&gt;</code> that you would write by hand. The set is always
    explicit; for two sets on a page, you hydrate each subtree with its own.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={vanillaHydrate} label="HTML" note="write the name, not the <svg>" />
  <CodeBlock code={vanillaBind} label="once, at startup" note="mountIcons; initComponents() does not call it" />
  <p>
    A <code>data-sk-icon</code> that the set does not cover is left intact and a warning is given: the geometry of the
    <strong>project</strong> is not a role, and is written as <code>&lt;svg&gt;</code> itself.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={vanilla} label="own geometry, by hand" note="for a drawing that no set has" />

  <h2>Accesibilidad</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Without <code>label</code> the icon is decorative</strong>, it has
      <code>aria-hidden="true"</code>. This is the normal case: in a button with text, the text already names the
      action.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>On an icon-only button, the accessible name is button</strong>
      (<code>aria-label="Close dialog"</code>), not <code>&lt;svg&gt;</code>. The icon inside
      remains decorative.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>With <code>label</code> the icon is content</strong>, <code>role="img"</code> more
      <code>aria-label</code>. Only when the icon stands alone and means something on its own.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>focusable="false"</code> always: a <code>&lt;svg&gt;</code> is not a tab stop.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Size</h2>
  <p>
    Three values of <strong>un</strong> hook. <code>--sk-icon-size</code> is density invariant: the
    density is spacing; an icon is contained next to a glyph — if the text does not shrink, the icon
    neither.
  </p>
  <Showcase html={sizeHtml} react={sizeReact} label="Icon · sm / md / lg" />
  <CodeBlock code={sizesCss} label="arbitrary size" note="no numeric prop" />
</Base>
